{#
    A blader's events in order, newest first, each one opening onto its matches.

    <twig:EventFeed :events="career.timeline" seasonSlug="{{ season.slug }}" />

    The feed is the match history rather than a summary of it: every match the
    blader played is inside one of these panels, grouped by the stage it was
    played in. `<details>` is native, so the whole history is reachable with
    JavaScript switched off — the one script this site ships may not be
    load-bearing, and a match log nobody can open without it would be.

    The recent few are what anybody came for, so the rest fold away behind a
    second `<details>`. Sixteen events is a long scroll before the points table
    on a phone, and every panel is already a `<details>`: the fold costs one more
    tap and nothing else, and what it hides is still the whole history rather
    than a link to somewhere else.
#}
{% props events = [], seasonSlug = null, initial = 3 %}

{# The loop variable is named away from the row's own `event` prop: inside a
   component's content its props are rebound, and a loop variable sharing the
   name is the collision AGENTS.md warns about. #}
<ol {{ attributes.defaults({class: 'space-y-2'}) }}>
    {% for entry in events|slice(0, initial) %}
        <twig:EventFeedRow :event="entry" seasonSlug="{{ seasonSlug }}" />
    {% else %}
        <li class="text-sm italic text-ink-faint">No events recorded.</li>
    {% endfor %}

    {% if events|length > initial %}
        <li>
            <twig:Disclosure summary="{{ events|length - initial }} earlier events" tone="neutral" compact>
                <ol class="space-y-2 py-2">
                    {% for entry in events|slice(initial) %}
                        <twig:EventFeedRow :event="entry" seasonSlug="{{ seasonSlug }}" />
                    {% endfor %}
                </ol>
            </twig:Disclosure>
        </li>
    {% endif %}
</ol>
